  "meta": {
    "status": "live",
    "notes": "The Overseas Circuit: florida-keys's career map (run W-R; interview, 2026-10-02: \"Network map, tiered\" and \"The map\"). Playtest 3 (T10.1; the maintainer, 2026-10-03: \"The progression doesn't feel right\"; round 3, \"Six bikes\", \"Gentle climb\"): sixteen nodes, four tiers of three regular events and the tier's boss (two wins open the boss, beating it opens the next tier; tier four's boss is Mother Rust). Each tier carries its field level (the pace share of the best bike open, aggression, signature gap, health and power, and which bike the rivals ride), the shop sells the Rustbucket, the Moped, the Sport 600 (tier two) and the Streetfighter (tier four), and the Superbike is San Francisco's. Wins claim roads and open the next ones; secrets are a shortcut, the region's pirate station (its route fraction, as the audio lane places it) and a stash of cash. Hurricane Chrome is the first season paint (open from Season 2). [default] every number.",
    "provenance": {
